  "event:evt.gen_16.sarai_proposes": {
   "status": "approved",
   "produced_by": {
    "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
    "skill": "urim-chronologist@5",
    "run": "main"
   },
   "produced_at": "2026-11-02T13:50:04+00:00",
   "agent_notes": [
    "Dated by 16:3 'at the end of ten years of dwelling in Canaan': Abram left Haran at 75 (12:4), so 75 + 10 = 85 years from anchor.abraham_birth; 16:16 (86 at the birth, nine months after conception) forces the proposal to about 85.25-85.9, so I used 85.4 with a 6-month margin. Gen 15 events sit at c. 2087 BCE in the corpus (they are anchored otherwise), i.e. about 6 years before this date on the birth-anchor count; the two chains disagree, I kept the age arithmetic here and did not tie Gen 16 to the Gen 15 events. Verse 1 is background (Sarai childless, Hagar) and joins this event; Targum Pseudo-Jonathan adds that Hagar was Pharaoh's daughter, which I did not use."
   ],
   "history": [
    {
     "status": "changes_requested",
     "at": "2026-11-02T13:49:24+00:00",
     "note": "[should_fix] Date the proposal so that both verses hold: e.g. offset 85.5 years from anchor.abraham_birth with a margin of about 6 months, and say in the note that 16:16 narrows the ten-year mark of 16:3. If the birth is instead anchored on abraham_birth at 86, check that the conception chain still lands within a few months of nine before it. (GEN.16.3: \"מִקֵּץ עֶשֶׂר שָׁנִים לְשֶׁבֶת אַבְרָם בְּאֶרֶץ כְּנָעַן\"; GEN.16.16: \"בֶּן־שְׁמֹנִים שָׁנָה וְשֵׁשׁ שָׁנִים\")",
     "by": "urim-critic@3 · claude-opus-5-5"
    },
